cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "cookie-consent-validator: a command line test for whether cookie banners honour rejection"
abstract: "Node.js command line tool that drives a real browser, clicks 'Reject All' on a site's consent banner, waits for the banner to be dismissed, then measures what survived: tracking cookies still set, tracker requests still firing, and web-storage keys matching known tracker patterns. Built to measure the gap between a banner that looks compliant and one that behaves as it claims. Recognises the common consent management platforms and exits non-zero when violations are found."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "TrustYourWebsite"
    website: "https://trustyourwebsite.com/eu/en"
repository-code: "https://github.com/trustyourwebsite/cookie-consent-validator"
url: "https://trustyourwebsite.github.io/cookie-consent-validator/"
license: MIT
version: "1.2.0"
keywords:
